  "worked_solution": "Both the numerator and denominator are factored. Now we cancel the common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(a) & =\\frac{5a-10}{(a-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5(a-2)}{(a-2)(a-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cancel{(a-2)}}{\\cancel{(a-2)}(a-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{a-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the numerator equal to zero, we get $5=0,$ which is a false statement. Therefore, $g(a)=0$ has no solution.",
